      "body": "Closes #6665\n\nFixes the filtered-query hole in the shard consumer for #6665 (task 13981).\n\n## Problem\n`ShardedBackend::branch_pools` sent the vector branch to `fanout_scan`, which refuses session-level filters loudly (scan shards carry no sessions or labels). So any hybrid/vector query with `--kind/--topic/--project/--client/--since/--until` against the shard core failed outright, even though the wrapped monolith can answer it correctly.\n\n## Change (`pkgs/atlas-search/crates/atlas-core/src/shards/scan.rs`)\n- When session-level filters are present, both branches are routed to the wrapped monolith, which evaluates the filters and the sensitivity ceiling in its own branch construction (ceiling preserved on the fallback).\n- A diagnostic naming the applied filters is recorded during `branch_pools` and surfaced via `notes()` — `run_search` folds late notes in, so the fallback appears in the search envelope.\n- Unfiltered vector queries keep the exact shard fan-out; FTS already stayed on the monolith (shards have no `chunks_fts`).\n- `fanout_scan` still refuses filtered queries loudly for direct callers.\n\nDecision recorded per #6665 acceptance: session-label filters stay on the monolith until cutover (no cross-store pushdown — that stays with #6664/#5668), and keyword/FTS search's home remains the monolith.\n\n## Tests\n- New: `sharded_backend_routes_filtered_queries_to_the_monolith` — filtered hybrid + vector-only queries take both pools from the monolith (exactly one inner call carrying both branches), the diagnostic note names the filters, and `fanout_scan` still refuses the same filters.\n- `cargo test -p atlas-core`: all 65 tests pass (incl. 12 shard tests). Re-verified fresh by lane code-m (task 13981 resume) 2026-11-09: 65 passed, 0 failed. `cargo fmt --check` clean for the touched files (pre-existing fmt diffs in `local.rs`/`turso.rs` untouched). Clippy not installed on the build host.\n\n<!-- agent-note:v1 agent=repo-worker-code lane=code-e state=pr_opened task=13981 -->\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796792208&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7954&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7954&signature=7de887ae95ecd3f148f58d21f826f5d5a3dbfae676cd1905b8c29eb957d3783d\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7954?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
